# Lifecycle.CreditHours module (P4.A) — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup (Development), same as users.http:
#   dotnet user-secrets set ConnectionStrings:Portal "Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=nimi_portal;Username=postgres;Password=<password>" --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity
#   dotnet user-secrets set SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL "admin@cu.edu.eg" --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity
#   dotnet user-secrets set SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD "<a password>" --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity
# Run:  dotnet run --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity          (migrations apply on startup in Development)
#
# Prerequisites: run scheduling.http first (faculty, department, term, CS301/CS303, groups, slots).
# Paste the ids/tokens it produced into the variables below; log in a student and a professor for their tokens.
# Calendar: first term 2026/2027 runs Saturday 2026-09-19 → Friday 2027-01-15. Product days: 0 = Saturday … 6 = Friday.
# Registration: decision D2 — auto-approved, every rule enforced; seats are an atomic counter (a full group is a 409).

@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminEmail = admin@cu.edu.eg
@adminPassword = paste-SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD-here

@termId = paste-term-id
@cs301 = paste-CS301-subject-id
@cs303 = paste-CS303-subject-id
@cs303GroupId = paste-CS303-group-id
@studentToken = paste-student-access-token
@professorToken = paste-professor-access-token

### 1. Log in as the seeded admin → copy "accessToken" into @token
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2. Open the term's registration window (one per term; credit limits default to 12/21)
# @name window
POST {{host}}/api/admin/registration-windows
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "termId": "{{termId}}",
  "opensAt": "2026-09-15T08:00:00Z",
  "closesAt": "2027-01-14T18:00:00Z",
  "minCredits": 12,
  "maxCredits": 21
}

###
# @name windows
GET {{host}}/api/admin/registration-windows?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Move it (or close it) while keeping the term:
PUT {{host}}/api/admin/registration-windows/{{windows.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "opensAt": "2026-09-15T08:00:00Z",
  "closesAt": "2027-01-14T18:00:00Z",
  "minCredits": 12,
  "maxCredits": 21
}

### 3. Prerequisites: CS303 requires CS301 (send the whole list; empty [] clears it)
PUT {{host}}/api/admin/registration/prerequisites/{{cs303}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "prerequisiteSubjectIds": ["{{cs301}}"] }

###
GET {{host}}/api/admin/registration/prerequisites/{{cs303}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. What the student can register this term (seats, slots, reasons; 404 without an active term)
GET {{host}}/api/registration/offerings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 5. Register a group, then read it back (409 when the group is full or the subject is already taken)
# @name registration
POST {{host}}/api/registration
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subjectGroupId": "{{cs303GroupId}}" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/registration/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 6. Drop it while the window is open (204; the seat goes back)
DELETE {{host}}/api/registration/{{registration.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 7. Roster for the teaching professor (admin can read any group's roster at /api/admin/groups/{id}/roster)
# Replace the id with the group's id; the professor must be assigned to the subject (or that group).
GET {{host}}/api/teaching/groups/{{cs303GroupId}}/roster?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### 8. The student's own week (same range rules and item shape as the teaching schedule)
GET {{host}}/api/schedule?from=2026-09-19&to=2026-09-25
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 8b. The same week as an Excel-friendly CSV (UTF-8 with BOM) — P10.4
GET {{host}}/api/schedule/export?from=2026-09-19&to=2026-09-25
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 9. Progress: credits earned and GPA (from published grades, P9), in progress now, outstanding graduation requirements
GET {{host}}/api/registration/progress
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
